  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "unkn_box_read",
    "file": "gpac/src/isomedia/box_code_base.c",
    "description": "The root cause is a type confusion in unknown-box parsing: `unkn_box_read` may parse the unknown box payload as sub-boxes (`gf_isom_box_array_read(s, sub_bs)`) and, on success, frees `ptr->data` and leaves `s->child_boxes` populated, but it does not change the box deleter/registry away from `unkn_box_del`. During teardown, `gf_isom_box_del` calls `unkn_box_del` (freeing the `GF_UnknownBox` object), then recursively deletes `child_boxes`, whose entries include pointers into/aliasing the already-freed parent object for this PoC path, leading to an invalid/double free seen in ASan (`gf_free` from `unkn_box_del`).",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires an input that creates an `unknown`/UUID box whose payload is heuristically accepted as nested boxes (first bytes look like plausible box header, e.g. PoC UUID data), so `unkn_box_read` enters the sub-box parsing path and keeps parsed children. On file close (`gf_isom_close` -> `gf_isom_delete_movie`), recursive box destruction (`gf_isom_box_del`/`gf_isom_box_array_del`) invokes `unkn_box_del` in an unsafe ownership state, causing free of an invalid pointer and ASan SEGV in allocator deallocation logic."
  },
